.TH "sudoconsole" "1" "Aug 2026" "sudoconsole " "sudoconsole Manual"

.SH NAME
sudoconsole-policy-test - Dry-run a command against the active policy


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsudoconsole policy test "" [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
test evaluates a command line against the effective policy and
prints the resulting decision (allow / warn / block / audit) together
with the matched categories, risk level and reasons. Nothing is
executed.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for test


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--cache-timeout\fP=0
	sudo cache timeout in seconds (60-3600); overrides config file

.PP
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the TOML config file (default: platform XDG/Application Support location)

.PP
\fB--format\fP=""
	output format: human or json (overrides config file)

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP=""
	log level: silent, error, warn, info, debug (overrides config file)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  sudoconsole policy test "ssh user@host"
  sudoconsole --format json policy test "apt update"
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsudoconsole-policy(1)\fP


